<title>USA: Big Flower slips after larger offering.</title>
<headline>Big Flower slips after larger offering.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Big Flower Press Holdings Inc slipped slightly in heavy trading on Wednesday morning after the company sold shares in a secondary offering.</p>
<p>Shares slipped 7/8 to the offering price of 21. The stock was the second most active issue on the New York Stock Exchange with about 1.5 shares traded an hour into the session</p>
<p>The New York advertising and and marketing services company focuses on personalized direct mail products. It increased the offering to sell 5.96 million shares from its first estimate of five million, according to lead underwriter Goldman Sachs.</p>
